1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:15,940
As you were doing this research, did you draw any connections to what would be the reason why Black people would be sequestered into these spaces and not given the opportunity to have the same as the other groups?

2
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:22,280
I mean, for me, the simple answer is like white supremacy. And I hate that it's to me, it's that simple.

3
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:28,700
But I think that people forget that like America was quite literally founded on the human trafficking of Black people.

4
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:37,120
And then as soon as that human trafficking ended, we developed an apartheid system to segregate and kind of denounce the humanity of Black people once again.

5
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:47,720
All of the addendums we see, the amendments we see are focused on controlling, using, extracting resources and capital from Black people.

6
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:59,020
You recognizing your own humanity is one of the most powerful political acts and you have to be committed to it at all times because they're either going to be entertained by watching you die or by watching you do something superhuman.

7
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:04,720
And you got to decide if that's how you want to go about the rest of your life. But I can't do that. Personally, I can't.

8
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,720
I just feel like a proud auntie.

9
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,280
Oh, I can tell. Thank you.

10
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:19,440
They don't know. Like we go back from, I think I first met you when I was like six or five years old at a grassroots give thanks event in Newark.

11
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,780
Yeah. Like, yeah, it was all the way back.

12
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:30,880
I was doing some appearance, you know, for the kids and coming to hang out with the kids.

13
